The prospective minimal target retains exactly the source-normalized V/kappa assumptions and the existing measurable-family conventions: all finite complete real Hilbert/Borel E, measurable S, measurable eta and y, and every eta(s)>0. No eta≤1 restriction is introduced: the small-step restriction in nearby Lemma4.1 belongs to its own bound. Unit specialization recovers fixed source parameters. The measurable-family and rank0 cases are authored interface extensions, not printed paper scope claims. No admissible reference-point premise is needed for this local analytical leaf; algorithm/reference/cost assumptions remain in their own later targets.

Definitions stay literal: mu=volume.tilted(-V); R_s=mu.tilted(-norm(x-y_s)²/(2eta_s)); r_s is its actual affine pushforward by (sqrt eta_s)^-1*(x-p_s); gamma=stdGaussian E; rho is the source Bregman remainder with the negative linear term. No repaired/proxy posterior or abstract Fisher certificate replaces these objects. The actual rho-energy equals the smooth relative-score energy because32 gives gradient(log q)=-gradient rho pointwise. Canonical llr itself is only identified AE under r and is not differentiated pointwise.

